Summary of changes

Branding and artwork
  Product, module and window names, the About page, the first-run welcome
  copy, the application, installer and Linux desktop icons, and the installer
  identity (application ids, package and artifact names) carry the UniWork
  Office brand. Code identifiers, package scopes, the genoffice command line,
  environment variable names and font family names keep their upstream names.

Privacy and network services
  The usage-analytics tracker and its consent prompt were removed. Links to
  the upstream source repository and the repository star prompt were removed
  from the interface. Account, credit top-up and download links point at
  UniWork services, and the update feed is configured at build time.

Work and practice features
  Practice packs for business roles, the UniWork Office Bridge client and its
  contracts, the UniAI web app, UniWork sign-in and cloud documents, and a
  Workbench with additional Home panes (tasks, calendar, notes, forms and
  others) were added. Vietnamese copy was revised throughout.

Packaging metadata
  The copyright, maintainer, vendor, author and homepage of the installers
  name UniWork. LICENSE, NOTICE, this file and the third-party notices ship
  inside the application and open from Settings > About.

Tooling
  A rebranding script with a brand scan (tools/rebrand) re-applies these
  changes after each upstream update, and tools/legal keeps NOTICE, this file
  and the package metadata in line with apps/shell/src/shared/legal.json.
